Rubric in Rhyme
Judge first the aim: is purpose clear, no fog, no haze;
Then image: can the scene be seen, felt on the skin;
Hear music: meter, beat, and ring that please the ear;
Scan line breaks: do cuts reveal, not mar the sense;
Test diction: crisp, exact; fat pared to lean;
Seek freshness: trite turns shunned, surprise alive;
Mark metaphor: apt links, no muddle in the mix;
Taste tone: true, steady, fitting theme and mood;
Trace arc: a path from seed to fruit by last line;
Check form: if set form stands, keep pact and art;
Prize economy: each line must earn its keep;
Note syntax: glide and pivot aid the gaze;
See shape: stanza frame aids breath and pace;
Grade impact: does some ember stay alight inside?
End test: does a single pass beget return?

